  "provenance": [
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2025_Topps_Series_1_BB_Checklist_-_updated.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-05",
      "covers": "Series 1 (#1-350) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Card #4 name repaired from interleaved PDF text ('Christian Encarnacion-StraCnindcinnati Reds' -> 'Christian Encarnacion-Strand' + 'Cincinnati Reds', deterministic rightmost-subsequence removal), as was the Tokyo Series first-game card. Three non-card sections skipped: Mystery Redemption Autograph Card, Social Media Follow Back Redemption and Fanatics Authentic Redemption Cards."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2025ToppsSeries2BaseballChecklist6-3.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-05",
      "covers": "Series 2 (#351-700) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Two non-card sections skipped: Social Media Follow Back Redemption and Fanatics Authentic Redemption Cards. Cards #365, #409 and #639 print a league where the team would go (Major League Baseball, National League), which is why those values are in teams.json."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "community",
      "source": "Baseball Card Pedia, 2025 Topps",
      "source_url": "https://baseballcardpedia.com/index.php/2025_Topps",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-05",
      "covers": "the factory set cards and which parallels cover every base card",
      "notes": "Confirms 66 of the 67 checklists it lists once the two series are summed; the exception is Legendary Homefield Advantage, counted 5 per series where the Topps PDFs print LHA-1 to LHA-5 and LHA-6 to LHA-9, so the manufacturer stands. Sole source for the two Factory Set checklists here, which are in neither series PDF. It states \"All 700 base cards are available in the following parallels\" and lists 42, recorded here as coverage: full. It qualifies Black as Series Two only, which the repo owner corrected: Black prints all 700. Names are taken from base.csv rather than from this source, which prints \"Colby Mayo\" for Topps' Coby Mayo at #20. Its KRC designation on the short-print rookies is not adopted: Topps prints \"Rookie\", and the kayfabe idea it marks is a category, recorded as a tag. It lists Printing Plates as one entry, \"set of four for each card\". They are declared as four — Black, Cyan, Magenta, Yellow — because a plate is a distinct one-of-one card a collector owns, and one entry cannot record owning the cyan plate of a given card. The count is this source's; the four colour names are the standard printing set, and TCDB names 2026's plates exactly so. Its Big Apple checklist prints #658 Gleyber Torres where the Topps Series 2 PDF prints #656 Jairo Iriarte in that section; the manufacturer's card stands. The 99 they agree on match exactly."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manual-transcription",
      "source": "Repo owner, from the cards",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-06",
      "covers": "True Photo and Team Color Border as full base parallels; the 582 Montgomery Club factory set parallel",
      "notes": "Both print all 700 base cards in 2025 and are declared coverage: full on that assertion alone. Baseball Card Pedia omits them from its list of parallels covering the whole base set, while listing Vintage Stock and Clear, which print all 700 the same year. Its 2026 page says of all four \"after years as full parallels, the following are now 200-card partial-parallels\", so the omission is that list being incomplete rather than these two being partial in 2025. The 582 Montgomery Club factory set, sold to club members, prints every base card with a sublimated 582 Club logo, so it is declared coverage: full. The box itself is not declared as a packaging: a packaging lists checklist files it contains and this one holds a parallel, which has no file, so the schema cannot yet say what is in it."
    }
  ],
